        "description_text": "Acer palmatum 'Beni hime' Japanese Maple Zones 5-9 Acer palmatum 'Beni Hime' is a dwarf Japanese Maple prized for its compact size and vivid red foliage. Over a span of 10 years, it typically grows to about 3-4 ft in height and 2-3 ft in width. Its petite stature makes it perfect for small gardens, containers, or bonsai cultivation. The leaves are small and deeply lobed, displaying a striking red hue that remains vibrant throughout the season. In autumn, the foliage transforms into a brilliant scarlet before falling. 'Beni Hime' features a dense, rounded growth habit with a bushy, compact form, developing a charming mound-like shape. 'Beni hime' is a tree that can be very difficult to grow and is not for a beginner. One tip we can give is to make sure you have very good drainage for this tree.",
